      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riesbach"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "From 1882 to 1896, the horse‑drawn Rösslitram connected Riesbach with Zürich’s main railway station.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riesbach"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Riesbach hosts historic medical sites such as the 1870‑established Burghölzli psychiatric hospital and the 1886 Swiss Epilepsy Centre.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riesbach"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The name Riesbach first appears around 930 in a deed granting land to the Grossmünster.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.zunft-riesbach.ch/gemeinde-riesbach"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Seefeldstrasse, built 1836‑1839 after the city walls fell in 1834, became a key artery for Riesbach.",
